        "note_tsim": [
            "Relief shown by shading",
            "Shows title at upper centre",
            "Shows lettered key (A-U) at lower right identifying the position of the troops",
            "Shows scale at lower right, \"NB The scale 200 Yards to one Inch\".",
            "Compare another manuscript map of the same (by a different hand?) - Add Ms 57,715.5",
            "Compare the manuscript \"Plan of the position which the army under Lt. Genl. Burgoyne took at Saratoga, on the 10th of September 1777, and in which it remained till the convention was signed\" held by the Library of Congress (Call Number G3803.S3S3 1777 .P5)",
            "Compare examples of the map published by William Faden (referenced in Nebenzahl, Kenneth. A bibliography of printed battle plans of the American Revolution, number 57).",
            "Copy at Add Ms 27,715.4. Manuscript inscription in black ink at upper right shows \"Presented by Colonel Sir Augustus Frazer K.C.B. R.A.\". Manuscript \"4\" added in pencil at upper right and \"265\" (crossed through) at lower centre. Laid on linen. Evidence of old folds. Green circular label to verso showing \"14\". White label to verso showing \"DRAWER 30 SECTION 3\". Blue label to verso showing \"A 30/14\". Manuscript addition of \"A 30/14\" in pencil to verso. Labels show \"290\". Manuscript annotations to verso in ink show \"Positions of Gen Burgoyne\" and \"Gen: Burgoyne's Position\"."
        ],
